Subject: [PATCH 4/4] 0296 dsv41: the decode KV fetch's distinct-picks-by-depth
 counter under TF_DS_ROUND_PROFILE

Instrumentation only (no new switch, no behavior change): every decode fetch's distinct picks
across the window's rows - the row count a decode union fetch would carry instead of rows x kk -
counted with the prompt union's own kernels (shard_ops.unionCount, shard.UnionRef's host model)
and tallied by the round's depth (its context bucket, floor-log2 bands), one JSON line a run in
the round profile (kv_pick_union, cumulative: native's /metrics print and the batch driver's
--profile). Sizes the decode KV union fetch against its 0.22-0.32 ms/forward ceiling; the gate
for the union-fetch patch brief is distinct / picks under a half at depth 32768 and 131072
(runs/trace-review-20261123/RESULTS.md section 4). A fetch of a selection counted already in
the round (a run's later layers: the same FetchKey) copies that count; the counts stay on the
device and are read back after the round's own sync, the ring probes' pattern. Off unless the
round profile is on (Model.useClock sets the gate).
